---
description: Directory tables size to content width/height; no viewport min-height stretch
globs: src/components/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Directory Table Sizing

Directory/list table cards grow with their rows. Do **not** stretch them to the
viewport for visual consistency when content is short.

## Width

- The table `Card` fills the **main content column** (sidebar + page padding
  already frame the layout).
- Do not target `100vw` / full browser width.

## Height

- Height is **content-first**: grow with rows; allow normal page scroll when the
  table is taller than the viewport.
- Empty and in-table loading states use the shared `DataTable` block
  (`px-6 py-12`). Standalone loaders/empty messages inside a table card should
  match (`px-6 py-12`).
- Do **not** set `min-h-[100vh]`, `min-h-screen`, or magic offsets like
  `min-h-[calc(100vh-…)]` on directory wrappers or table cards just to make
  sparse pages look “full.”

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — content-sized shell (same as customers / vehicles / items)
<div>
  <PageHeader … />
  <Card className="mt-6 gap-0">…</Card>
</div>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fake viewport height when few rows
<div className="flex min-h-[calc(100vh-11rem)] flex-col">
  <Card className="mt-6 gap-0">…</Card>
</div>
```

## Exceptions (do not use these as excuses for directory stretch)

- **Dashboard shell** may keep a page-level `min-h` so the main region fills
  under the header — that is not a table rule.
- **Maps / form tab shells / full-screen dialogs** may use definite viewport
  height when the UI needs an internal scroll region.
- **Fill remaining height + internal body scroll** (sticky toolbar, scrollable
  rows, pinned pagination) is allowed only when explicitly building that shell
  with a definite remaining space — not via a hardcoded viewport `min-h` on a
  short content card.

## Checklist

- [ ] No directory/table card or workspace wrapper uses viewport `min-h` for look
- [ ] Table card still uses `mt-6 gap-0` (see `table-header-divider-spacing`)
- [ ] Empty/loading inside the card uses `py-12` (or `DataTable` empty slot)
